A sprite naming a freed atlas texture is skipped instead of panicking.

A cached view replays the primitives it painted last, so a sprite can
outlive the texture behind it when an image is dropped before that view
repaints. `c3-remove-asset-drops-textures` frees textures as soon as an
asset goes. In the crash that prompted this, two atlas pages holding
now-playing covers were freed a second before a frame indexed one of them
and `BladeAtlasStorage`'s `unwrap` took the app down. `get_texture_info` now answers None for a
freed texture, the renderer skips that batch for the frame, and the first
miss per texture logs a warning naming it so the early drop can be found.
Blade only: Metal and DirectX keep their own atlases.

Diffed against the tree with every earlier patch applied.

